WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.200
-Enjoy yourself.
Thank you.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.400
Welcome, everybody.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.667
Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.667 --> 00:00:06.000
You're here.
You made it.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:09.033
Thank you
for watching at home, too.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.834
Guys, I want to say congrats
to the Kansas City Chiefs

00:00:11.834 --> 00:00:14.367
on winning the Super Bowl.

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:15.701
That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:17.400
[ Discordant celebration music
plays ]

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.434
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:19.834
-Wow!
-Sorry.

00:00:19.834 --> 00:00:22.501
Sorry -- sorry, Roots.
-[ Groans ]

00:00:22.501 --> 00:00:25.100
-Tariq is really
laughing it up tonight.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.534
Yeah.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:32.567
The final score
was Chiefs, 38, Eagles, 35.

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:35.234
People who called out sick
to work, 19 million.

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.367
-Oh.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.367 --> 00:00:38.200
That's right.
Today, a record 19 million

00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.767
Americans were expected
to miss work.

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.868
Yep. We all woke up this morning
and chugged Gatorade

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.534
as if we actually played
in the game.

00:00:44.534 --> 00:00:45.868
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.100
That's right.
Patrick Mahomes won

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.634
the Super Bowl
on an injured ankle,

00:00:48.634 --> 00:00:49.968
but fans can't show up to work

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.400
because they drank
too much White Claw.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.801
[ Laughter ]

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.400
19 -- 19 million
people missed work.

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.467
Apparently, some of them used
a special excuse generator.

00:00:58.467 --> 00:00:59.801
Have you heard about it?
I'll show you how it works.

00:00:59.801 --> 00:01:01.601
For example,
when your boss asks,

00:01:01.601 --> 00:01:03.767
"Why didn't you come in today?",
it tells you to say...

00:01:03.767 --> 00:01:06.067
[ Beeping ]

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:09.000
"I tried, but on my way in,
my Tesla exploded."

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.200
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.000
It's -- It's any excuse.
-Yeah.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.234
-It helps you.

00:01:14.234 --> 00:01:16.701
Next up, when your boss asks,
"Well, then, why aren't you

00:01:16.701 --> 00:01:18.534
working remotely?", just say...

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.734
[ Beeping ]

00:01:20.734 --> 00:01:23.601
"My Internet is being blocked by
a Chinese spy balloon."

00:01:23.601 --> 00:01:26.734
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:29.033
-This is work.
-Yeah.

00:01:29.033 --> 00:01:30.501
-And, finally,
when your kids ask,

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.801
"Why do we have to go to school

00:01:31.801 --> 00:01:34.100
if you don't have to go
to work?", you just say...

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:36.434
[ Beeping ]

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:38.467
"You need good grades
to get a scholarship

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:40.534
because I lost your college fund
on DraftKings."

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:43.000
-Oh.
[ Applause ]

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:46.701
-Very helpful machine.
-Yeah, very helpful.

00:01:46.701 --> 00:01:47.934
-Did you guys see this?
Before the game,

00:01:47.934 --> 00:01:50.734
Chris Stapleton, amazing,
sang the national anthem.

00:01:50.734 --> 00:01:53.534
And during his performance,
Eagles coach Nick Sirianni

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:55.334
got a little emotional.
Take a look at this.

00:01:55.334 --> 00:02:01.367
♪ The bombs bursting in air ♪

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:05.901
♪ Gave proof ♪

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:09.667
-God only knows what he looked
like after they lost.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:11.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:14.868
Must've been a puddle
with a headset.

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:16.534
Meanwhile, everyone
was talking about this.

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:20.934
The NFL used a new type of grass
that took two years to prepare,

00:02:20.934 --> 00:02:23.100
and it was so slippery that
the players were falling down

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:26.100
on it the entire game.
Yeah, always smart to try

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:28.100
something new on the biggest
game of the year, I think.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:31.934
But the NFL actually released
a statement defending the grass.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:34.100
They said,
"This is way funnier."

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:38.133
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:02:38.133 --> 00:02:41.100
Funnier if they fall around.
"Whoa!"

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.300
"That's a good one."

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.167
One of the biggest moments
of the night, of course,

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:48.434
was Rihanna's amazing halftime
show that she did solo.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:54.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.267 --> 00:02:56.767
That she did solo.
Yeah, well, it turns out

00:02:56.767 --> 00:02:59.467
she did actually have a guest,
because during her performance,

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.868
Rihanna revealed
that she's pregnant.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:02.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:06.200
Yes.

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.434
Rihanna did a Super Bowl
halftime show while pregnant.

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.667
Meanwhile, everyone at home
on their 30th chicken wing

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:15.267
was like, "I also felt a kick."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:16.767
Imagine it's the first day
of kindergarten

00:03:16.767 --> 00:03:17.901
and your fun fact is that

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.601
you've done the Super Bowl
halftime show.

00:03:19.601 --> 00:03:21.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.534
Well, this is big.
Today, Rihanna announced

00:03:23.534 --> 00:03:25.734
that the gender reveal
will be at the Olympics.

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.734
-Aww.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:30.801
-I read that, last night,
a 30-second commercial spot

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:33.634
cost more than $7 million.

00:03:33.634 --> 00:03:35.067
Wow.
You plan it for months,

00:03:35.067 --> 00:03:37.667
pay a ton of money, then the big
moment's over in 30 seconds.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:43.367
It's basically Valentine's Day.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:44.968
-Oh!
-That's right.

00:03:44.968 --> 00:03:48.133
Tomorrow is Valentine's Day,
which means a lot of people

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.701
are exchanging cards,
including famous people.

00:03:50.701 --> 00:03:52.267
And I don't know how this
happened, but we actually

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:54.067
got ahold of
some of these famous --

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.167
-Really?
-Yes. Yeah, I don't kno--

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.734
-That's insane.
-Well, we get them --

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:57.934
We have a lot of people --
-How did you do it?

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.234
How did you get them?
-We have a lot of fans of

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.467
"The Tonight Show,"
people working for us...

00:04:01.467 --> 00:04:03.000
-Right.
-...finding these cards and...

00:04:03.000 --> 00:04:04.601
-Oh, my gosh.
-...getting it to us before

00:04:04.601 --> 00:04:06.601
the famous couple exchanges it.
-That's so great.

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:07.934
And you're gonna share them
with the audience?

00:04:07.934 --> 00:04:10.400
-I'd love to, if you don't mind.
-I'd love -- [ Laughs ]

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.601
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Is that okay?

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.133
Why not?
That's what I do.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:16.367
That's why I'm here.

00:04:16.367 --> 00:04:19.434
First, here's one that
Mike Pence sent to his wife.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.534
It says that, "You're the
only woman that's ever..."

00:04:21.534 --> 00:04:23.133
you open it up, it says,
"...seen me in my

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:25.167
full-body underwear."
-Aww.

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:26.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:29.067
-Romantic.

00:04:29.067 --> 00:04:30.934
Here's one
that Jay-Z sent to Beyoncé.

00:04:30.934 --> 00:04:33.300
It says, "I would do anything
for...", you open it up,

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.400
it says. "...tickets
to your upcoming tour."

00:04:35.400 --> 00:04:39.501
[ Cheers and applause ]
It's very hard to get.

00:04:39.501 --> 00:04:41.634
Here's one that Zach,
the Bachelor,

00:04:41.634 --> 00:04:43.467
sent to one of the contestants.
It says,

00:04:43.467 --> 00:04:45.968
"Katie, there's no one else
like you...", you open it up,

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.868
it says, "...aside from
the three other Katies

00:04:47.868 --> 00:04:49.434
I'm also dating."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:52.501
Besides that,
you're the only one.

00:04:52.501 --> 00:04:54.000
Here's -- I thought this one
was really nice.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.868
-Really?
-Here's one that Chiefs coach

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:58.801
Andy Reid sent to his wife.
It says, "Today, I gift you...",

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.400
you open it up, it says,
"...half a box of chocolates."

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
Isn't that nice?

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:06.400
[ Laughs ]

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.601
And finally,
here's one that Patrick Mahomes

00:05:08.601 --> 00:05:09.634
sent to his wife.

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.234
It says,
"I think about you all the time.

00:05:11.234 --> 00:05:13.634
You're my inspiration...",
you open it up, it says,

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:15.300
"Please deliver this card
to Tom Brady."

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:17.100
[ Laughter and applause ]
Roman-- It's romantic.

00:05:17.100 --> 00:05:22.300
See? Happy Valentine's Day,
everybody.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.133
Well, switching gears,
some political news.

00:05:24.133 --> 00:05:25.868
I heard that
the Biden administration

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:29.634
is likely going to block the
JetBlue-Spirit airlines merger.

00:05:29.634 --> 00:05:31.667
-Ooh.
-Yep, now all of JetBlue's

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.000
friends can be like, "Honestly,
we all hated Spirit."

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.167 --> 00:05:37.300
"Oh, you guys
are going back out?"

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.100
"Oh, we love Spirit.
Seriously."

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:40.968
That's right,
Biden's gonna stop the merger,

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.601
or as they call it
in the airline world,

00:05:42.601 --> 00:05:43.934
"a cockpit block."

00:05:43.934 --> 00:05:47.968
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.968 --> 00:05:49.300
-Wow.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:53.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:53.367 --> 00:05:55.200
-People --
People are talking about this.

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:58.200
I saw that an Italian restaurant
in New Jersey

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.868
is banning kids
under 10 years old.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:02.534 --> 00:06:05.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:05.267 --> 00:06:06.334
♪♪

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:10.067
What?

00:06:10.067 --> 00:06:11.534
It's New Jersey, so already,

00:06:11.534 --> 00:06:13.267
9 year olds
are sliding the hostess a $20

00:06:13.267 --> 00:06:15.334
like, "See what you can do.
All right?"

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.467 --> 00:06:22.434
Well, this is going viral.
A user on TikTok shared a story

00:06:22.434 --> 00:06:24.801
about how her boyfriend
found a rubber glove

00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:26.601
in his food at
The Cheesecake Factory.

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:28.234
[ Audience groans ]
Listen, if you're gonna find

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:29.534
something in your meal
that's rubber,

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:31.067
just be thankful it's a glove.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:33.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.901 --> 00:06:36.534
In a related story, plenty of
Valentine's Day reservations

00:06:36.534 --> 00:06:38.300
just opened up at
Cheesecake Factory,

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.067
so there you go.
You can get in.

00:06:40.067 --> 00:06:42.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

